---
type: agent/instruction
description: Hand an existing linked worktree to a fresh agent session
usage: "guide://_worktree/use/<worktree-name>"
minargs: 1
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
includes:
  - ../_partials/handoff-context-target
  - ../../_system/_handoff-context
---
{{>handoff-context}}

Using the current Git worktree inventory, read {{>handoff-context-target}}.
Locate `projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.{{args.0.value}}`. It must exist,
and its recorded absolute `path` must appear in the fresh Git worktree inventory.
If either check fails, do not allocate a replacement name or hand off a child;
refresh or repair the handoff entry first. Use its recorded resumable information
as the child handoff.

Before assigning the child, create or initialise the target worktree's effective
configured workflow file with `worktree: {{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, preserving
its workflow state. Retain the existing handoff entry under
`projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.

Give the child the worktree name `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, its absolute
recorded path, and the complete handoff entry. Do not forward this session
ID. The child must work from that path, create a fresh Guide interaction, bind
the shared project root and that worktree, then read its local workflow file
before workflow or handoff-context operations.
